BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Drafty) Tj T* () Tj T* (Drafty Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Every winter, millions of renters open a utility bill that is far higher than expected and have) Tj T* (no idea why. In older multifamily buildings, a large share of heating energy is lost through) Tj T* (leaky windows, gaps under doors, unsealed outlets and poorly insulated walls. Renters usually) Tj T* (pay the utility bill but do not own the building, so they are stuck. A professional energy) Tj T* (audit typically costs several hundred dollars, is designed for homeowners, and often ends in a) Tj T* (report that recommends upgrades a tenant cannot make. Small landlords, who own most rental) Tj T* (units in the country, have the opposite problem: they are responsible for the building but) Tj T* (rarely see the bills, so they have little data and little motivation to act.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We saw this ourselves. In a survey of 212 students and young renters at our university and) Tj T* (nearby neighborhoods, 78 percent said their winter heating costs were higher than expected, and) Tj T* (only 9 percent could name the cause. Residential energy costs also keep rising, which makes the) Tj T* (problem sharper each year. The result is wasted money, wasted energy and avoidable emissions,) Tj T* (with no simple tool to fix it.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Drafty is a sensor-and-app kit that maps heat loss in an apartment and tells the user what to) Tj T* (fix first. Each kit has six small wireless sensors that measure temperature, humidity and air) Tj T* (movement. The user places them at windows, doors, outlets and baseboards for about 48 hours and) Tj T* (pairs them with the app. Our software combines the readings with outdoor weather and basic) Tj T* (details about the unit, then produces a heat-loss map and a ranked list of fixes sorted by) Tj T* (cost, effort and estimated payback.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Most recommended fixes cost under 40 dollars and need no contractor or permission:) Tj T* (weatherstripping, door sweeps, outlet gaskets, window film, curtain changes. The app links to) Tj T* (the parts and gives short installation guides. After fixes are made, users can rerun the) Tj T* (sensors to see measured improvement, which is what makes Drafty different from a generic) Tj T* (checklist. Landlords can also use a portfolio dashboard to compare units and prioritize) Tj T* (repairs.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The United States has about 44 million renter households. Most pay at least part of their own) Tj T* (energy costs. We focus first on renters in older multifamily buildings in cold and mixed) Tj T* (climates, roughly 12 million households. If a quarter of them bought one kit at our planned) Tj T* (price, the one-time hardware market alone would be above 100 million dollars, before recurring) Tj T* (landlord subscriptions. The second segment is small landlords, owners of one to twenty units,) Tj T* (who hold a large share of rental housing and are underserved by existing energy tools. We) Tj T* (estimate about 2 million such owners nationwide.) Tj T* () Tj T* (A third, longer-term segment is utilities and city energy programs, which are required in many) Tj T* (states to meet efficiency targets and pay for measurable savings. Our anonymized data on where) Tj T* (homes lose heat is valuable to them.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We earn money in three ways. First, we sell the sensor kit directly to renters for 59 dollars.) Tj T* (Our current cost of goods is about 24 dollars per kit at small volume, and we expect it to fall) Tj T* (below 18 dollars when we order at scale. Second, we sell a landlord subscription at 6 dollars) Tj T* (per unit per month, which includes the portfolio dashboard, repeat scans each season and a) Tj T* (prioritized repair plan. Third, we plan to license anonymized, aggregated building data to) Tj T* (utilities and efficiency programs. Affiliate revenue from recommended parts adds a small) Tj T* (additional margin.) Tj ET
endstream
