BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td () Tj T* (Sensors are reusable, so a single kit can be lent between units or reused each year, which) Tj T* (lowers the cost for landlords and keeps subscription customers engaged.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our competitors fall into three groups. Professional energy auditors give detailed results but) Tj T* (cost hundreds of dollars and serve homeowners. Smart thermostats and general home sensors) Tj T* (collect data but do not diagnose heat loss or recommend fixes. Free online checklists and) Tj T* (utility tips are cheap but generic and do not tell a renter what is wrong in their particular) Tj T* (apartment. Thermal-camera attachments for phones exist, but they need skill to interpret and) Tj T* (only show surface temperature at one moment.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Drafty is built for renters and small landlords, costs a fraction of an audit, and gives a) Tj T* (ranked, apartment-specific action list with measured before-and-after results. Our advantage is) Tj T* (the combination of low-cost hardware with analysis software, and the data we collect with every) Tj T* (scan will make our recommendations more accurate over time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Maya Okonkwo-Reyes, our CEO, is a senior in environmental policy who ran the renter survey and) Tj T* (leads customer development and partnerships. Daniel Whitfield, our CTO, is a senior in) Tj T* (electrical engineering who designed the sensor hardware and firmware. Priyanka Venkataraman,) Tj T* (our head of data, is a master's student in data science who built the heat-loss model and the) Tj T* (ranking engine. Tomas Brandt, our head of product, is a junior in industrial design who leads) Tj T* (the app and kit design. We are advised by a faculty member in building energy systems and a) Tj T* (retired property manager with thirty years of experience in small multifamily buildings.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have defined the core concept, built a working prototype of the kit and app, and put it in) Tj T* (front of outside users. Over the last winter we ran Drafty in 41 apartments. Of these, 27 users) Tj T* (paid for the kit at a discounted pilot price, and one local property manager with 60 units) Tj T* (signed a paid pilot for 12 units. In follow-up scans, users who completed at least three) Tj T* (recommended fixes measured an average 14 percent reduction in temperature loss at problem) Tj T* (points, and self-reported bills dropped by an estimated 8 to 12 percent. Our app is live and) Tj T* (our website collects signups, with a waitlist of over 400 people.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have not yet formed a legal entity and plan to incorporate in the coming months. To date we) Tj T* (have spent about 9,000 dollars, mostly on parts and prototypes, funded by pilot revenue and a) Tj T* (small university grant. Pilot revenue so far is about 2,300 dollars. We project 85,000 dollars) Tj T* (in revenue in the first full year, mostly from kit sales and landlord pilots, rising to roughly) Tj T* (420,000 dollars in year two as subscriptions grow and we add our first utility data pilot.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are seeking 40,000 dollars in prize or seed funding. About half would go to our first) Tj T* (production run of 800 kits and certification testing, 30 percent to app development and our) Tj T* (data pipeline, and the rest to legal formation, insurance and marketing to landlords. Beyond) Tj T* (funding, we would value introductions to property management associations, utility program) Tj T* (contacts and mentors with hardware manufacturing experience. With this support we expect to) Tj T* (complete incorporation, double our landlord pilots, and be ready for a public launch ahead of) Tj T* (next winter.) Tj ET
endstream
